592186436463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436453 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436454 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436459 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436461 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1077 "selection" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436453 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436463 1079 #uuid "7879cf33-2aec-51b3-9623-83b7a16a99c7" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436448 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436449 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436451 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436457 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1075 #edb/ref 17592186436458 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1077 "selection" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436449 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436464 1079 #uuid "efeb7b02-1be6-5efa-9bd8-eb3062a43a07" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436465 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436462 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436465 1069 "q-111104" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436465 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436465 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436465 1072 #uuid "0f9d6921-1029-58c3-84e2-79c33a9e57b1" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436465 1074 "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k+2 \\\\ 4k-4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2k+2=0 \\\\ 4k-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=1.$" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436466 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436464 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436466 1069 "q-111115" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436466 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436466 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436466 1072 #uuid "312e3366-ac87-55a7-a43b-4cbe0aecef1d" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436466 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=3{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\\}.\n$$" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436467 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436463 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436467 1069 "q-34952" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436467 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436467 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -7 & 7\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436467 1072 #uuid "b6c9ad88-847a-5bc3-8131-a821e5ea8f1f" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436467 1074 "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -7 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-7){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}-{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436468 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436470 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436468 1062 #uuid "15381825-f698-53f0-84f0-2e86406279e2" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436468 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436465 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436469 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436472 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [17592186436469 1062 #uuid "29910b71-b3db-5759-85dc-176a6617f370" 13194139534800 17592186045417 true] [1759218